course: dictionary
lesson: 956
title: Blotchy: patches of colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blotchy means covered in blotches, which are uneven patches of colour. Think of a leopard's coat, or a face that has gone red in patches after a hard run. «After a long time standing half in shade and half in sun, the Giraffe grew blotchy» tells you his colour changed into uneven patches, not one even shade.
explain: Blotchy can describe things other than animals. «The Giraffe went to tallish trees where the shadows fell all blotchy.» Shadows are patches of dark, and the light falling through leaves makes them uneven. So blotchy is about patches that are not even, not just any spots.
explain: Check the words around blotchy. Words like striped, spotty and patchy sit near it in the story, and they all point to uneven marks. Then test your meaning: if «the shadows were uneven patches of dark» still makes sense in the sentence, you have it right.
fact: Blotchy means covered in blotches: uneven patches of colour.
fact: «Blotchy» can describe skin, paint, cloth, shadows or an animal's coat.
fact: Skin can go blotchy after crying, running or in the cold, or with a rash or an allergy.
fact: «Blotchy» is an adjective, and its forms are blotchy, blotchier and blotchiest.
fact: «Striped» means having lines of colour, while «blotchy» means having uneven patches. They are close, but they are not the same.
exercise: «The Giraffe grew blotchy, and the Zebra grew stripy.» What does blotchy mean? | Covered in straight lines of colour | Very tall and thin | *Covered in uneven patches of colour | Smooth and shiny all over
exercise: Ella's cheeks went blotchy after she cried. What does blotchy mean here? | *Her skin had uneven patches of colour | Her skin was completely smooth and pale | Her cheeks were cold and wet | Her face was hidden by her hands
exercise: Find and copy one word in «the striped and blotchy shadows» that means having uneven patches of colour. | shadows | *blotchy | and | striped
test: «After a long time standing half in shade and half in sun, the Giraffe grew blotchy.» What does this tell you about his coat? | It grew much longer | *Its colour became uneven, in patches | It became perfectly smooth | It turned bright blue
test: Mum says Sam's skin is blotchy after running. What does she mean? | Sam has run out of the house | *Sam's skin has red, uneven patches | Sam's skin is silky and smooth | Sam's hair is stripy
exam: Which sentence uses blotchy correctly? | The blotchy puppy slept quietly in a plain white box | She sang a blotchy song that made everyone clap | *The old wall looked blotchy, with patches of faded and darker paint | He ate a blotchy sandwich for lunch
